A||||7||Wannabe||Saw an Absolutely Gorgeous Fiero||||1||
Z||000000||Wannabe||10-05-2001||09:27 PM||||I'm generally not impressed by showy stuff, prefering to see what's going on in the hardware department, but this one is definitely worth mentioning. I have no idea if it belongs to a forum member, but I was at Fiero Shop in TO the other day and out front was an absolutely gorgeous Fiero convertible.  It was painted a metallic maroon color and had a tan leather interior - everything including the seats and the door panels was covered in soft leather. Apparently the car is a 4 cyl (a real let down in the hardware department) '97 convert. with '88 rims. It also had a woodgrain dash kit that went very well with the leather treatment. It had only 44,000 miles on it and the owner aparently paid about $10KCDN (about $6500US) for it. Whoever you are, good buy, and beautiful car! ||||reg||1
